  "review_notes": [
    "The verse writes לֹא יוּכַל twice and the ASV renders it two ways: the first as the indivisible cannot, which rule 35 keeps as one unit with the verb, and the second as not ... be able, which the same rule splits.",
    "בְּשֶׁל is one three-morpheme fusion on because, and however much is read as אֲשֶׁר's own rendering; the four supplied object pronouns and the second yet answer to no morpheme and are added."
  ]
